solution:
**Given:**

Rohit made a profit of 22% when he sold a jacket for ₹7,930.

Selling Price (SP) = ₹7,930

Profit Percentage = 22%

**Formula used:**

Cost Price (CP) = dfrac{SP}{1 + dfrac{Profit \%}{100}}

**Calculations:**

CP = dfrac{7930}{1 + dfrac{22}{100}}

⇒ CP = dfrac{7930}{1 + 0.22}

⇒ CP = dfrac{7930}{1.22}

⇒ CP = ₹6,500

**∴ The correct answer is option (1).**
